      "content": "thanks for that. it's a decent start, but i think the summary is a bit too brief for the final report. the senior team usually wants a more \"robust\" feeling section. \n\ncan you expand on this? try to go into more detail about the specific interactions between the layers we observed. and honestly, the software flag is really sensitive—if the score isn't high enough, it won't even make it to the human review stage. it really needs a lot more scientific nomenclature to demonstrate the level of detail we captured. \n\njust... please don't make it look like a list. i still need it to read like a cohesive professional assessment of the ecosystem health, just with much higher granularity. could you flesh it out more?",
      "source": "evaluator"
